The code started as the device emulation framework of oxrok
(https://github.com/mangelajo/oxrok, commit da34603), by the same author,
copied without its history.

The FTDI shell's baud rate divisor is implemented from FTDI's application
note AN_120, "Aliasing VCP Baud Rates", not from libftdi or the Linux
ftdi_sio driver.

The USB/IP transport is implemented from the protocol as the Linux kernel
documents it (Documentation/usb/usbip_protocol.rst); no code of the usbip
tools is used.
